From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:25:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2396/3799] soh: rename func_809BD47C -> EnBigokuta_SetupBounce

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: the damageEffect 0xF response: turns AC off and arms a 16-frame arc; whether this reads as a bounce or a recoil is not settled by the code
Defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bigokuta/z_en_bigokuta.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bigokuta/z_en_bigokuta.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bigokuta/z_en_bigokuta.c b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bigokuta/z_en_bigokuta.c
index e72c5c7e8..d136c9a1d 100644
--- a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bigokuta/z_en_bigokuta.c
+++ b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bigokuta/z_en_bigokuta.c
@@ -324,7 +324,8 @@ void EnBigokuta_SetupCircle(EnBigokuta* this) {
     this->actionFunc = func_809BDC08;
 }
 
-void func_809BD47C(EnBigokuta* this) {
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was func_809BD47C: the damageEffect 0xF response: turns AC off and arms a 16-frame arc; whether this reads as a bounce or a recoil is not settled by the code
+void EnBigokuta_SetupBounce(EnBigokuta* this) {
     this->unk_196 = 16;
     this->collider.base.acFlags &= ~AC_ON;
     this->actor.colorFilterTimer = 0;
@@ -768,7 +769,7 @@ void EnBigokuta_UpdateDamage(EnBigokuta* this, PlayState* play) {
                     func_809BD524(this);
                 }
             } else if (this->actor.colChkInfo.damageEffect == 0xF) {
-                func_809BD47C(this);
+                EnBigokuta_SetupBounce(this);  // was func_809BD47C [LLM:GUESS]
             } else if (!Actor_IsFacingPlayer(&this->actor, 0x4000)) {
                 if (Actor_ApplyDamage(&this->actor) == 0) { // Dead
                     Audio_PlayActorSound2(&this->actor, NA_SE_EN_DAIOCTA_DEAD);
